      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I was just making a little joke, but I suppose it's not entirely clear. You see, goblins are notorious for their love of mischief and mayhem, and they often find creative ways to get into tight spots. In this case, I was just using the phrase to add a bit of whimsy to the conversation. But, of course, I'm sure your luggage is perfectly safe and goblin-free.\n\nNow, about the rules: if you arrive late for your train, you can still check in your luggage, but you'll need to do so at the designated check-in points, and you'll need to pay any applicable fees. If your bags are slightly over the weight limit, you can still bring them on board, but you may be asked to weigh them at the gate or at the luggage carousel, and if they exceed the limit, you may be required to check them in or pay a fee.\n\nIt's also worth noting that the Eurostar has a \"smart luggage\" policy, which means that if your luggage is equipped with a GPS tracking device, you can track its location in real-time, and if it's lost or delayed, you can receive notifications. It's a great way to keep an eye on your belongings",
